# Caddy configuration for running BOTH classroom apps on ONE machine
# (e.g. a Raspberry Pi 4) with TWO DuckDNS hostnames and free HTTPS.
#
#   https://mybookrecs.duckdns.org    -> Book Recs         (localhost:8080)
#   https://myroomlibrary.duckdns.org -> Classroom Library (localhost:8081)
#
# Only ONE Caddy runs on the machine: it owns ports 80+443 and routes each
# hostname to its app. Caddy fetches and renews both Let's Encrypt
# certificates automatically. Full walkthrough: deploy/dual-host-pi.md
#
# SETUP
#   1. Copy this file to  Caddyfile  (same folder is fine for `caddy run`,
#      or /etc/caddy/Caddyfile if Caddy runs as a system service).
#   2. Replace the two hostnames below with YOUR real DuckDNS hostnames.
#   3. Book Recs must listen on 8080, Classroom Library on 8081.
#      The systemd units pin this (BOOKRECS_PORT / CLASSROOM_PORT) so the
#      ports can never drift into each other — see deploy/dual-host-pi.md.
#   4. Router: forward external 443 -> this computer -> 443
#      AND external 80 -> this computer -> 80 (cert renewals use port 80).
#   5. Run:  caddy run   (or: sudo systemctl enable --now caddy)
#
# Only hosting Book Recs on this machine? Use Caddyfile.example instead.

mybookrecs.duckdns.org {
	reverse_proxy localhost:8080
}

myroomlibrary.duckdns.org {
	reverse_proxy localhost:8081
}
